p8Brief:
Lily — a preschooler, little girl of average build with auburn wavy chin-length loose hair uncovered, wearing a yellow top under a green quilted gilet, dark blue corduroy trousers, and orange boots — sits on the damp cobbles inside the dark timber nook, her back to the log pile, both feet flat on the ground, arms braced behind her, head tilted back slightly as she blinks up at Ethan. Ethan — a young school-age boy of average build with dark brown curly short hair, brown eyes, and a rounded jawline, wearing a blue anorak, white top, dark grey jeans, and brown boots — kneels in front of her, gripping her left wrist with his right hand, leaning forward with knees planted, eyes narrowed, teeth gritted, his left hand resting on the cobbles beside her hip for balance. Lily’s chunky red woollen hat lies on the cobbles just in front of her right foot, fully visible, the only vivid colour in the gloom. Behind them, the narrow gap of the log pile is visible, a top log tipped diagonally across the opening, its bark rough and grey-brown. The fading dusk light outlines the log pile and the timber frame of the Holzbrücke bridge mouth. Medium shot.

