p3Brief:
Lily — a preschooler, little girl of average build with auburn wavy chin-length loose hair parted on the left, brown eyes, a soft jawline, and freckles, wearing her red chunky-knit woollen hat, a yellow top under a green quilted gilet, dark blue corduroy trousers, and orange rubber-soled boots — springs forward out from behind a large stone rubbish bin in the left foreground of the open stone-paved square, her eyes wide, mouth open in a shriek of excitement, her legs bent mid-leap. A few paces away in the right midground, caught fully in the open, a girl of about five — small and slight with black fringed hair, dark brown eyes wide with shock, mouth slightly open, wearing a red duffel coat with wooden toggles, dark navy tights, and black velcro-strap shoes — stands completely frozen, her arms pinned rigidly to her sides. In the far distance on the right, roughly a sixth their size, a boy of about ten — slightly tall and lean, light brown short hair, pale grey eyes, wearing a dark charcoal puffer jacket, a striped red-and-white scarf wound twice around his neck, dark green trousers, and black trainers — stands in side profile, his brow furrowed in concentration, eyes closed as he counts aloud, his back partially turned to the tower wall. Copper-coloured fallen chestnut leaves scatter across the grey cobbles under a pale grey overcast sky. Ultra-wide shot.

